{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Ascendancy and The War Within combine aggressive riffs with melodic leads and hooks, which makes them natural next choices after my In Flames and Soilwork listening.",
    "Vol. 3 fits the heaviness and melody I enjoyed in Ten Thousand Fists, while As The Palaces Burn appeals to the more intense, riff-driven side of my listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Darkest Days leans toward industrial rock when I want guitar-driven metal; a heavy sound alone does not make it the right fit today.",
    "St. Anger's raw, repetitive approach does not give me the melodic riffs I want, while True Parallels fits my broader taste but feels less compelling during this heavier listening session."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat heaviness and aggression as enough to connect albums, even though the riffs, melodies and overall feel affect my choices.",
    "My past hard rock listening seems to carry too much weight for what I want now; liking The Reason and One Day Remains does not mean I would prioritize similar albums today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The combination of melodic leads and aggressive guitar riffs matters especially strongly right now, which is why Ascendancy stands out.",
    "An album can fit my taste without making me want to choose it immediately: Skeletons, Confession and Avenged Sevenfold interest me, but the strongest matches take priority."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy music, but sometimes miss which combinations of melody, riffs and intensity make me want to listen now."
}"}
